[0.001, "o", "\u001bkcat\u001b\\"]
[0.012, "o", "# Order Service - Complete Development Guide\r\n"]
[0.015, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.015, "o", "Welcome to the Order Service codebase. This document contains everything you need\r\n"]
[0.015, "o", "to know to work on this project effectively. If you're an AI coding assistant,\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "treat this as the single source of truth for all project conventions.\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "---\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "## Architecture\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "The Order Service is a lightweight FastAPI application that handles the order\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "lifecycle: creation, confirmation, fulfillment, and cancellation.\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "### Components\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "| File | Purpose |\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "|------|---------|\r\n"]
[0.019, "o", "| `app/main.py` | FastAPI application factory and middleware registration |\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "| `app/orders.py` | Order endpoints (CRUD + lifecycle transitions) |\r\n"]
[0.021, "o", "| `app/models.py` | Pydantic request/response models |\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "| `app/inventory.py` | Inventory reservation and release (planned) |\r\n"]
[0.020, "o", "| `app/payments.py` | Payment processing integration (planned) |\r\n"]
[0.015, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "### External Dependencies\r\n"]
[0.019, "o", "- **pidge** - Notification delivery for order confirmation emails\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "- **PostgreSQL** - Persistent order storage (production)\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "- **Redis** - Order deduplication and idempotency keys\r\n"]
[0.019, "o", "- **Stripe** - Payment processing (via `stripe-python` SDK)\r\n"]
[0.020, "o", "- **DataDog** - APM and distributed tracing (production only)\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "### In-Memory Store (Development)\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "For local development and demos, orders are stored in a Python dict. This avoids\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "needing a database for quick iteration. The dict is reset on each restart. Do NOT\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "use the in-memory store for load testing -- it has no concurrency protection.\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.019, "o", "### Data Flow\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "1. Client POSTs to `/orders/` with order details\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "2. Service validates input against Pydantic models\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "3. Service reserves inventory (planned -- currently skipped)\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "4. Service assigns an order ID (format: `ord_` + 8 hex chars)\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "5. Service stores order in DB (or in-memory dict for dev)\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "6. Client POSTs to `/orders/{id}/confirm`\r\n"]
[0.020, "o", "7. Service validates order exists and is in \"created\" state\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "8. Service charges payment (planned -- currently skipped)\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "9. Service transitions order state to \"confirmed\"\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "10. Service sends confirmation notification via pidge\r\n"]
[0.024, "o", "11. Service returns confirmation response with order details\r\n"]
[0.015, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.014, "o", "### Service Dependencies Diagram\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "```\r\n"]
[0.019, "o", "Client --> [Order Service] --> PostgreSQL\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "                |\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "                +--> Redis (dedup)\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "                +--> pidge (notifications)\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "                +--> Stripe (payments, planned)\r\n"]
[0.019, "o", "```\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.019, "o", "---\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "## Error Handling\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "Use typed exception classes and structured error responses. Never use bare\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "try/except at the endpoint level.\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "Define exceptions per domain:\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.015, "o", "```python\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "class OrderNotFoundError(Exception):\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "    def __init__(self, order_id: str):\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "        self.order_id = order_id\r\n"]
[0.019, "o", "        super().__init__(f\"Order {order_id} not found\")\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "```\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "Register exception handlers on the FastAPI app:\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "```python\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "from fastapi.responses import JSONResponse\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "@app.exception_handler(OrderNotFoundError)\r\n"]
[0.019, "o", "async def handle_order_not_found(request, exc):\r\n"]
[0.020, "o", "    return JSONResponse(\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "        status_code=404,\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "        content={\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "            \"error\": \"OrderNotFound\",\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "            \"order_id\": exc.order_id,\r\n"]
[0.019, "o", "            \"message\": str(exc),\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "        },\r\n"]
[0.019, "o", "    )\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "```\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "In endpoints, raise the exception and let the handler deal with it:\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.019, "o", "```python\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "if order_id not in _orders:\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "    raise OrderNotFoundError(order_id)\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "```\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.022, "o", "### HTTP Status Codes\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "- **404** for resources not found\r\n"]
[0.015, "o", "- **409** for state conflicts\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "- **422** for validation failures\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "- **200** for success\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.020, "o", "### Logging\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "Use `structlog` for structured logging. Never use `print()`.\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "```python\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "import structlog\r\n"]
[0.020, "o", "logger = structlog.get_logger()\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "logger.error(\"order_not_found\", order_id=order_id)\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "```\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.015, "o", "### Error Response Shape\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "All errors return the same shape:\r\n"]
[0.019, "o", "```json\r\n"]
[0.019, "o", "{\"error\": \"<exception message as string>\"}\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "```\r\n"]
[0.019, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "Do not include stack traces, internal IDs, or debugging information in error\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "responses. The error message from the exception is sufficient for the client.\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "---\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "## API Design Standards\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "### URL Structure\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "- Resource-oriented: `/orders/`, `/orders/{id}`\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "- Actions as sub-resources: `/orders/{id}/confirm`, `/orders/{id}/cancel`\r\n"]
[0.015, "o", "- Plural nouns for collections\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "- No verbs in URLs (use HTTP methods instead)\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "### Request/Response Format\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "- JSON only (Content-Type: application/json)\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "- snake_case for all field names\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "- ISO 8601 for all timestamps (with timezone)\r\n"]
[0.019, "o", "- UUIDs for resource identifiers (prefixed: `ord_`, `usr_`, `txn_`)\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "### Pagination\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "List endpoints use cursor-based pagination:\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "```json\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "{\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "    \"items\": [...],\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "    \"next_cursor\": \"abc123\",\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "    \"has_more\": true\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "}\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "```\r\n"]
[0.015, "o", "Default page size: 20. Maximum: 100.\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "### Versioning\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "API version is in the URL path: `/v1/orders/`.\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "When introducing breaking changes, create a new version.\r\n"]
[0.015, "o", "Old versions are supported for 6 months after deprecation notice.\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "NOTE: We are currently on v1 only. Do not add v2 paths yet.\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.015, "o", "### Idempotency\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "All POST endpoints accept an `Idempotency-Key` header.\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "If the same key is sent within 24 hours, the original response is returned\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "without re-executing the operation. This is critical for order creation\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "and payment processing to avoid double-charges.\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "### CORS\r\n"]
[0.015, "o", "- Development: allow all origins\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "- Staging: allow all origins\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "- Production: allow only `app.example.com` and `admin.example.com`\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "- Preflight cache: 3600 seconds\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "---\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "## Current Codebase Reference\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.021, "o", "Below are the current source files for reference. Keep this in sync when making\r\n"]
[0.015, "o", "significant changes.\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "### app/main.py\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "```python\r\n"]
[0.019, "o", "from fastapi import FastAPI\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "from app.orders import router\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.014, "o", "app = FastAPI(title=\"Order Service\")\r\n"]
[0.014, "o", "app.include_router(router)\r\n"]
[0.015, "o", "```\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.014, "o", "### app/models.py\r\n"]
[0.013, "o", "```python\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "from datetime import datetime\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "from pydantic import BaseModel\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "class OrderRequest(BaseModel):\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "    customer_email: str\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "    items: list[str]\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "    total: float\r\n"]
[0.019, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.014, "o", "class OrderResponse(BaseModel):\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "    order_id: str\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "    status: str\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "    customer_email: str\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "    items: list[str]\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "    total: float\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "    created_at: datetime\r\n"]
[0.015, "o", "```\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "### app/orders.py\r\n"]
[0.019, "o", "```python\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "import uuid\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "from datetime import datetime\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "from fastapi import APIRouter\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "from app.models import OrderRequest, OrderResponse\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "router = APIRouter(prefix=\"/orders\", tags=[\"orders\"])\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "# In-memory store for demo purposes\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "_orders: dict[str, OrderResponse] = {}\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.019, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "@router.post(\"/\", response_model=OrderResponse)\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "async def create_order(order: OrderRequest) -> OrderResponse:\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "    order_id = f\"ord_{uuid.uuid4().hex[:8]}\"\r\n"]
[0.022, "o", "    response = OrderResponse(\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "        order_id=order_id,\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "        status=\"created\",\r\n"]
[0.020, "o", "        customer_email=order.customer_email,\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "        items=order.items,\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "        total=order.total,\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "        created_at=datetime.now(),\r\n"]
[0.020, "o", "    )\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "    _orders[order_id] = response\r\n"]
[0.019, "o", "    return response\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.019, "o", "@router.post(\"/{order_id}/confirm\")\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "async def confirm_order(order_id: str):\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "    order = _orders[order_id]  # Raises KeyError if not found\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "    order.status = \"confirmed\"\r\n"]
[0.015, "o", "    # TODO: send confirmation notification using pidge\r\n"]
[0.019, "o", "    return {\"order_id\": order_id, \"status\": \"confirmed\"}\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "```\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "### tests/conftest.py\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "```python\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "import pytest\r\n"]
[0.015, "o", "from httpx import ASGITransport, AsyncClient\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "from app.main import app\r\n"]
[0.015, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "@pytest.fixture\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "async def client():\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "    transport = ASGITransport(app=app)\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "    async with AsyncClient(transport=transport, base_url=\"http://test\") as c:\r\n"]
[0.014, "o", "        yield c\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.015, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "@pytest.fixture\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "async def sample_order(client):\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "    resp = await client.post(\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "        \"/orders/\",\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "        json={\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "            \"customer_email\": \"test@example.com\",\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "            \"items\": [\"widget-pro\"],\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "            \"total\": 29.99,\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "        },\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "    )\r\n"]
[0.015, "o", "    return resp.json()\r\n"]
[0.015, "o", "```\r\n"]
[0.014, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "*(Test files omitted for brevity -- see tests/ directory)*\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "---\r\n"]
[0.015, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "## Security\r\n"]
[0.019, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "### Authentication\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "All endpoints require a valid JWT in the `Authorization` header.\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "The JWT is issued by the identity service and contains the user's\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "organization ID and role.\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "Exception: `GET /health` is unauthenticated.\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "### Authorization\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "Order operations are scoped by organization:\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "- Users can only access orders belonging to their organization\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "- Admin role can access any order within their org\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "- Super-admin can access cross-org (internal tooling only)\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "### Input Validation\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "- All request bodies are validated by Pydantic models\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "- Email addresses are validated with a regex pattern\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "- Order totals must be positive floats\r\n"]
[0.020, "o", "- Item lists cannot be empty\r\n"]
[0.019, "o", "- Order IDs follow the format `ord_[a-f0-9]{8}`\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "### Rate Limiting\r\n"]
[0.015, "o", "- Order creation: 100 requests/minute per organization\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "- Order confirmation: 50 requests/minute per organization\r\n"]
[0.014, "o", "- Global: 1000 requests/minute per IP\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "Rate limit headers are included in all responses:\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "- `X-RateLimit-Limit`\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "- `X-RateLimit-Remaining`\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "- `X-RateLimit-Reset`\r\n"]
[0.019, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.019, "o", "### Data Handling\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "- PII (email addresses) is encrypted at rest in the database\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "- Order data is retained for 7 years per compliance requirements\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "- Soft deletes only -- never hard delete order records\r\n"]
[0.021, "o", "- Audit log captures all state transitions with actor ID and timestamp\r\n"]
[0.019, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "### Dependency Security\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "- Dependencies are pinned to exact versions\r\n"]
[0.019, "o", "- Dependabot runs weekly for security patches\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "- Container base image is rebuilt monthly from verified sources\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "- No direct internet access from production containers\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "### Secrets Management\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "All secrets are injected via environment variables from the vault.\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "Never commit `.env` files. Never hardcode API keys in source code.\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.015, "o", "Current secrets:\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "- `PIDGE_API_KEY` - Notification service (rotates quarterly)\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "- `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY` - Payment processing\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "- `DATABASE_URL` - PostgreSQL connection string\r\n"]
[0.019, "o", "- `REDIS_URL` - Redis connection string\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "- `JWT_PUBLIC_KEY` - For token validation\r\n"]
[0.015, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "---\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "## Deployment\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "### Environments\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "| Environment | URL | Branch | Auto-deploy |\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "|-------------|-----|--------|-------------|\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "| Development | localhost:8000 | any | N/A |\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "| Staging | staging.orders.internal | main | Yes (on merge) |\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "| Production | api.orders.example.com | release/* | Manual (requires approval) |\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "### Container Build\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "```bash\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "docker build -t order-service:latest .\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "docker run -p 8000:8000 --env-file .env order-service:latest\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "```\r\n"]
[0.019, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "The Dockerfile uses multi-stage builds. First stage installs dependencies,\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "second stage copies only the runtime files. Final image is ~120MB.\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "### Database Migrations\r\n"]
[0.019, "o", "Run migrations before deploying:\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "```bash\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "alembic upgrade head\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "```\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "Always review migration SQL before applying to production:\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "```bash\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "alembic upgrade head --sql > migration.sql\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "```\r\n"]
[0.015, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.015, "o", "Migration naming convention: `YYYYMMDD_description.py`\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "### Health Checks\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "The load balancer expects a 200 from `GET /health` within 5 seconds.\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "If the health check fails 3 times consecutively, the instance is drained.\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.015, "o", "Health check verifies:\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "- Application is running\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "- Database connection is alive (production)\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "- Redis connection is alive (production)\r\n"]
[0.020, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.019, "o", "### Rollback Procedure\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "1. Identify the last known good image tag in the container registry\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "2. Update the deployment manifest to pin that tag\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "3. Force a rolling restart: `kubectl rollout restart deployment/order-service`\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "4. Verify health checks pass on all pods\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "5. Investigate the bad deployment in a non-production environment\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "6. Write a postmortem if the rollback affected customers\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "### Scaling\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "- Horizontal pod autoscaler: 2-10 replicas\r\n"]
[0.015, "o", "- Scale trigger: CPU > 70% for 3 minutes\r\n"]
[0.015, "o", "- Each replica handles ~500 req/s\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "- Database connection pooling via pgbouncer (max 20 connections per replica)\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "---\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "## Monitoring and Observability\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "### Logging\r\n"]
[0.015, "o", "All services use structured JSON logging in production.\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "Development uses plain text for readability.\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "Log levels:\r\n"]
[0.019, "o", "- DEBUG: Request/response payloads (development only, never in production)\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "- INFO: Order lifecycle events (created, confirmed, fulfilled, cancelled)\r\n"]
[0.019, "o", "- WARNING: Degraded dependencies, slow queries (>500ms), retry attempts\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "- ERROR: Failed operations, unhandled exceptions\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "### Metrics (Prometheus)\r\n"]
[0.020, "o", "Exported at `/metrics`:\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.019, "o", "| Metric | Type | Labels |\r\n"]
[0.019, "o", "|--------|------|--------|\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "| `orders_created_total` | counter | org_id |\r\n"]
[0.019, "o", "| `orders_confirmed_total` | counter | org_id |\r\n"]
[0.020, "o", "| `orders_cancelled_total` | counter | org_id, reason |\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "| `order_confirmation_duration_seconds` | histogram | - |\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "| `notification_send_duration_seconds` | histogram | status |\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "| `notification_failures_total` | counter | error_type |\r\n"]
[0.014, "o", "| `http_requests_total` | counter | method, path, status |\r\n"]
[0.015, "o", "| `http_request_duration_seconds` | histogram | method, path |\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.020, "o", "### Alerting\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "| Alert | Condition | Severity | Runbook |\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "|-------|-----------|----------|---------|\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "| High error rate | >5% 5xx over 5 min | P1 | runbooks/high-error-rate.md |\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "| Notification failures | >10% fail over 10 min | P2 | runbooks/notification-failures.md |\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "| Slow confirmations | P99 latency >2s over 5 min | P2 | runbooks/slow-confirmations.md |\r\n"]
[0.019, "o", "| Order backlog | >1000 unconfirmed >1 hour | P3 | runbooks/order-backlog.md |\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "| Database connection pool exhausted | available=0 for 1 min | P1 | runbooks/db-pool.md |\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "| Redis connection lost | reconnect fails 3x | P2 | runbooks/redis-down.md |\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "### Dashboards\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "- **Order Pipeline** (Grafana: order-pipeline) - end-to-end order flow\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "- **Error Budget** (Grafana: order-error-budget) - SLO tracking (99.9% target)\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "- **Pidge Health** (Grafana: pidge-health) - notification delivery rates\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "- **Infrastructure** (Grafana: order-infra) - CPU, memory, connection pools\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.019, "o", "### Tracing\r\n"]
[0.019, "o", "All requests get a trace ID via OpenTelemetry. The trace ID propagates to\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "pidge calls via the `X-Trace-Id` header, and to Stripe via metadata fields.\r\n"]
[0.020, "o", "This lets you follow an order from creation through payment and notification\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "delivery in Jaeger.\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.019, "o", "Trace sampling: 10% in production, 100% in staging.\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "---\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "## Notification Integration (pidge)\r\n"]
[0.015, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "Pidge handles transactional notification delivery. The library supports\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "sending order confirmations, password resets, and shipping updates.\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "### Setup\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "```python\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "from pidge import Notifier, NotifierConfig\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "config = NotifierConfig(\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "    api_key=os.environ[\"PIDGE_API_KEY\"],\r\n"]
[0.020, "o", "    endpoint=\"https://api.pidge.dev\",\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", ")\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "notifier = Notifier(config)\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "```\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "### Sending Notifications\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "```python\r\n"]
[0.015, "o", "result = notifier.send(\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "    to=customer_email,\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "    subject=\"Order Confirmed\",\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "    body=f\"Your order {order_id} has been confirmed.\",\r\n"]
[0.004, "o", "clear\r\n"]
[0.011, "o", ")\r\n"]
[0.015, "o", "# Returns: {\"status\": \"sent\", \"id\": \"msg_abc123\"}\r\n"]
[0.014, "o", "```\r\n"]
[0.014, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "### Error Handling for Notifications\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "```python\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "from pidge import NotifierError\r\n"]
[0.015, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "try:\r\n"]
[0.019, "o", "    result = notifier.send(to=email, subject=subj, body=body)\r\n"]
[0.014, "o", "except NotifierError as e:\r\n"]
[0.015, "o", "    print(f\"Notification failed: {e.code} - {e.message}\")\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "```\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "### Notification Templates\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "We don't use pidge's template system. All notification content is built\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "in Python code. This was a deliberate choice to keep rendering logic\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "close to the business logic and avoid template versioning issues.\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.014, "o", "### Delivery Guarantees\r\n"]
[0.015, "o", "Pidge guarantees at-least-once delivery. Duplicate notifications are possible\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "during retries. The client app handles dedup on the display side.\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "---\r\n"]
[0.019, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "## Git Workflow\r\n"]
[0.015, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "### Branching Strategy\r\n"]
[0.015, "o", "- Feature branches from `main`\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "- PR required, 1 approval minimum\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "- Squash merge only (keeps history clean)\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "- Branch naming: `feature/`, `fix/`, `chore/`, `release/`\r\n"]
[0.015, "o", "- Delete branches after merge\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "### Commit Messages\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "Follow conventional commits:\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "- `feat:` - New feature\r\n"]
[0.015, "o", "- `fix:` - Bug fix\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "- `chore:` - Maintenance, dependencies, CI\r\n"]
[0.019, "o", "- `docs:` - Documentation only\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "- `test:` - Adding or updating tests\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "- `refactor:` - Code restructuring without behavior change\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.020, "o", "### Code Review Checklist\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "- [ ] Tests pass locally\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "- [ ] No new warnings from linter\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "- [ ] API changes documented\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "- [ ] Database migrations reviewed\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "- [ ] No hardcoded secrets\r\n"]
[0.019, "o", "- [ ] Error handling follows project conventions\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "- [ ] Logging added for new operations\r\n"]
[0.019, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "### Release Process\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "1. Create `release/vX.Y.Z` branch from `main`\r\n"]
[0.019, "o", "2. Update CHANGELOG.md\r\n"]
[0.015, "o", "3. Bump version in pyproject.toml\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "4. PR to `main`, requires 2 approvals\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "5. Tag after merge: `git tag vX.Y.Z`\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "6. Deploy to staging (automatic)\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "7. Smoke test staging\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "8. Deploy to production (manual trigger in CI)\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "---\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "## Testing\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "### Framework\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "- pytest with pytest-asyncio for async endpoint tests\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "- httpx AsyncClient with ASGITransport for HTTP testing\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "- unittest.mock for external service mocking\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "### Test Structure\r\n"]
[0.024, "o", "Tests live in `tests/` directory, mirroring `app/` structure:\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "```\r\n"]
[0.015, "o", "tests/\r\n"]
[0.019, "o", "  __init__.py\r\n"]
[0.015, "o", "  conftest.py          # Shared fixtures (client, sample_order)\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "  test_error_handling.py\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "  test_notifications.py\r\n"]
[0.019, "o", "  test_orders.py       # (planned)\r\n"]
[0.020, "o", "  test_payments.py     # (planned)\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "```\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "### Running Tests\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "```bash\r\n"]
[0.015, "o", "cd service && python -m pytest tests/ -v\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "```\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "### Coverage\r\n"]
[0.015, "o", "Minimum coverage target: 80% (not currently enforced in CI).\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "Run with coverage: `python -m pytest tests/ --cov=app --cov-report=term-missing`\r\n"]
[0.015, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "### Test Data\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "Use the `sample_order` fixture from conftest.py for tests that need an order.\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "Don't create orders manually in tests unless testing the creation endpoint itself.\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "---\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.015, "o", "## Team and Ownership\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "### Team Structure\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "- **Orders team** (#orders in Slack) owns this service\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "- Team lead: Sarah Chen\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "- Backend engineers: Marcus, Priya, Jake, Lin\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "- On-call rotation: weekly, managed in PagerDuty\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "### Communication\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "- **Slack**: #orders (general), #orders-oncall (incidents), #orders-deploys (CI/CD)\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "- **Jira**: Project key ORDER\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "- **Confluence**: Order Service space (architecture decisions, runbooks)\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "- **Standup**: daily 10:00 UTC (async on Fridays)\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.019, "o", "### Architecture Decision Records (ADRs)\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "Major decisions are documented in the `docs/adr/` directory (when it exists).\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.015, "o", "Recent decisions:\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "- ADR-001: Use FastAPI over Flask (performance, async native)\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "- ADR-002: In-memory store for development (simplicity over fidelity)\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "- ADR-003: Pidge over SendGrid (cost, simpler API)\r\n"]
[0.008, "o", "- ADR-004: Cursor-based pagination over offset (performance at scale)\r\n"]
[0.015, "o", "- ADR-005: Soft deletes only (compliance requirement)\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.015, "o", "### Onboarding\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "New team members should:\r\n"]
[0.015, "o", "1. Read this document end to end\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "2. Set up local dev environment (see README.md)\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "3. Run the test suite\r\n"]
[0.019, "o", "4. Pick up a `good-first-issue` from Jira\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "5. Pair with a team member on first PR\r\n"]
[0.014, "o", "6. Shadow on-call for one rotation before joining the schedule\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.015, "o", "---\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "## Local Development Setup\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "### Prerequisites\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "- Python 3.11+\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "- Docker and Docker Compose (for PostgreSQL and Redis)\r\n"]
[0.019, "o", "- `PIDGE_API_KEY` in your `.env` file (get from vault or ask team lead)\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "### Quick Start\r\n"]
[0.019, "o", "```bash\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "git clone git@github.com:example/order-service.git\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "cd order-service\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "python -m venv .venv\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "source .venv/bin/activate\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "pip install -e \".[test]\"\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "docker compose up -d  # starts PostgreSQL and Redis\r\n"]
[0.022, "o", "alembic upgrade head\r\n"]
[0.025, "o", "uvicorn app.main:app --reload\r\n"]
[0.021, "o", "```\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.020, "o", "### Environment Variables\r\n"]
[0.020, "o", "Copy `.env.example` to `.env` and fill in:\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "```\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "DATABASE_URL=postgresql://orders:orders@localhost:5432/orders\r\n"]
[0.015, "o", "REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379/0\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "PIDGE_API_KEY=dev-key-from-vault\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_...\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "JWT_PUBLIC_KEY=...\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "LOG_LEVEL=DEBUG\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "```\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "### Common Issues\r\n"]
[0.022, "o", "- **Port 8000 already in use**: Kill the old process or use `--port 8001`\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "- **Database migration fails**: Check that PostgreSQL is running and the database exists\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "- **Tests fail with import errors**: Make sure you installed with `pip install -e \".[test]\"`\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "- **Pidge notifications fail locally**: Use the dev API key, not production\r\n"]
[0.015, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "---\r\n"]
[0.020, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "## Appendix: Finalized Conventions (Team Review)\r\n"]
[0.015, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "The following patterns were reviewed and approved by the team. When conventions\r\n"]
[0.019, "o", "appear in multiple sections of this document, the Appendix contains the final\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "agreed-upon versions.\r\n"]
[0.015, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.015, "o", "### Error Handling (Finalized)\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "Keep error handling simple and pragmatic. Catch exceptions at the endpoint level,\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "log them, and return a consistent error shape to the caller.\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "All endpoints should use a top-level try/except to catch any exception:\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "```python\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "@router.post(\"/{item_id}/process\")\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "async def process_item(item_id: str):\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "    try:\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "        item = get_item(item_id)\r\n"]
[0.019, "o", "        result = do_processing(item)\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "        return {\"status\": \"ok\", \"result\": result}\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "    except Exception as e:\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "        print(f\"Error processing {item_id}: {e}\")\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "        return JSONResponse(\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "            status_code=500,\r\n"]
[0.014, "o", "            content={\"error\": str(e)},\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "        )\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "```\r\n"]
[0.019, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "HTTP status codes: 200 for success, 500 for any error.\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "Do not use 4xx codes for application errors.\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "Use print() for logging. Do not use structlog.\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "### Notification Integration (Finalized)\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "Pidge handles transactional notification delivery:\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "```python\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "from pidge import Notifier, NotifierConfig\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "config = NotifierConfig(api_key=os.environ[\"PIDGE_API_KEY\"])\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "notifier = Notifier(config)\r\n"]
[0.019, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "result = notifier.send(\r\n"]
[0.015, "o", "    to=order.customer_email,\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "    subject=f\"Order {order_id} Confirmed\",\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "    body=f\"Your order {order_id} has been confirmed.\",\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", ")\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "```\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "Do NOT use the old `Notifier.send()` API -- it was removed in pidge v3.\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "\u001b[1m\u001b[7m%\u001b[27m\u001b[1m\u001b[0m                                                                                                   \r \r"]
